            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="0960" n="850" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg850"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1153 St 2/40: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-02-14T11:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 14,
                                1928—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 14—9:25
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>41. Reference to the Department’s 14, February 1, and 15, February 2, both to
                        Madrid.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d717-f1"/> Following consultations with Mr.
                    Blair en route from Madrid to London and back from there, where he was
                    encouraged by developments, the Spanish oil situation has been informally <pb
                        facs="0961" n="851" xml:id="pg851"/> discussed by this Embassy with the
                    French Foreign Office. The desirability of the French Embassy in London aiding
                    in bringing the British Government to favor concerted action was especially
                    suggested. I refer to the Department’s No. 2607 of February 2.<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d717-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
